WEBVTT

00:02.227 --> 00:03.861
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:05.363 --> 00:07.097
Are you eating
cookie dough?

00:07.099 --> 00:08.999
Yup. It's my favorite recipe.

00:09.001 --> 00:11.435
All you need
is cookie dough and weed.

00:11.437 --> 00:14.238
So the only thing
you have to bake is yourself.

00:14.240 --> 00:15.739
It's very efficient.

00:15.741 --> 00:19.009
It causes the munchies
and then immediately cures them.

00:19.011 --> 00:20.878
(computer chimes)
Hey.

00:20.880 --> 00:22.646
What do you know?
They found my car.

00:22.648 --> 00:24.114
You lost your car?

00:24.116 --> 00:26.183
What the hell's your
cookie dough laced with?

00:26.185 --> 00:28.018
No, I found this company

00:28.020 --> 00:31.021
and they help you
locate old vehicles.

00:31.023 --> 00:33.557
It's called
Dude, Where's My Car?

00:33.559 --> 00:35.426
So what's so great
about this thing?

00:35.428 --> 00:38.362
I don't know. It's my first car.
I got a lot of firsts in it.

00:38.364 --> 00:40.030
First time I learned to drive.

00:40.032 --> 00:42.666
First time I had sex.

00:42.668 --> 00:44.635
First time I had a condom break.

00:44.637 --> 00:46.904
First time I prayed.

00:46.906 --> 00:48.605
So you gonna buy this car?

00:48.607 --> 00:52.309
No. Some guy named
Dirk in Denver has it.

00:52.311 --> 00:53.510
So why go through all the effort

00:53.512 --> 00:55.279
of tracking it down
if you don't want it?

00:55.281 --> 00:56.680
Nostalgia?

00:56.682 --> 00:58.515
It's kind of like...

00:58.517 --> 01:00.217
looking up
your first girlfriend,

01:00.219 --> 01:02.052
or your high school
math teacher.

01:02.054 --> 01:05.289
For me,
those were one and the same.

01:05.291 --> 01:08.025
She still writes me
from prison.

01:09.060 --> 01:11.762
I think my math teacher
had a crush on my me, too.

01:11.764 --> 01:14.431
I mean, why else would he ask me
to take a shower

01:14.433 --> 01:16.166
after math team practice?

01:17.001 --> 01:18.936
Oh, oh, good, everybody's here.

01:18.938 --> 01:22.473
Uh, I would now like
to introduce my girlfriend,

01:22.475 --> 01:24.575
the very fetchin'
Gretchen.

01:24.577 --> 01:25.609
Hey, everybody.

01:25.611 --> 01:26.977
Hi, I'm Walden. It's nice

01:26.979 --> 01:28.378
to finally meet you.
Yeah.

01:28.380 --> 01:30.180
Alan, uh, told me that you work

01:30.182 --> 01:32.149
in an animal shelter
taking in strays.

01:32.817 --> 01:34.651
So we have
a lot in common.

01:34.653 --> 01:36.453
Yeah.

01:36.455 --> 01:37.988
Uh, this is my-my niece Jenny.

01:37.990 --> 01:38.989
Hi.
Hi.

01:38.991 --> 01:40.090
And we met.

01:40.092 --> 01:41.492
I'm Barry, Walden's
youthful ward.

01:41.494 --> 01:43.126
It's really nice
to meet all of you.

01:43.128 --> 01:44.361
God, this place
is amazing.

01:44.363 --> 01:46.029
How do you afford
the rent, Alan?

01:46.031 --> 01:48.298
(laughs)

01:49.167 --> 01:50.300
What's so funny?

01:50.302 --> 01:52.669
Well, I-I don't pay rent,
per se.

01:52.671 --> 01:54.071
Or per month.

01:55.073 --> 01:56.573
Or per year.

01:56.575 --> 01:58.742
Really? No rent?

01:58.744 --> 02:00.043
How long has that
been going on?

02:00.045 --> 02:02.179
Three years with Walden,
eight years with my dad.

02:02.181 --> 02:05.949
You have been living here
for 11 years for free?

02:05.951 --> 02:06.984
Yeah.

02:06.986 --> 02:08.585
I have never
wanted you more.

02:08.587 --> 02:09.686
(chuckles)

02:09.688 --> 02:11.421
Who's my cheap daddy?

02:11.423 --> 02:13.457
Would you like to see
the bedroom I don't pay for?

02:13.459 --> 02:16.360
Would you like to see my boobs
I bought with a Groupon?

02:18.296 --> 02:20.797
Will you let me get
my grope on?

02:21.933 --> 02:24.902
Nice to meet you, Gretchen.
Make yourself at home.

02:24.904 --> 02:26.770
I've got to stop
saying that.

02:26.772 --> 02:29.139
So, what do you say
we hop on your plane,

02:29.141 --> 02:31.642
head over to Denver
and at least look at this car?

02:31.644 --> 02:33.110
You know you want to.

02:33.112 --> 02:34.945
You guys just want
to go to Colorado

02:34.947 --> 02:36.079
'cause pot is legal there.

02:36.081 --> 02:38.615
What?
It's-It's legal?

02:38.617 --> 02:40.450
They legalized marijuana
in Colorado?

02:40.452 --> 02:43.520
You say up
to three ounces?

02:43.522 --> 02:46.423
Look, we're not going to Denver
to look at a car

02:46.425 --> 02:48.025
and bring home
three ounces of pot.

02:48.027 --> 02:49.860
Yeah, but if we go
with you,

02:49.862 --> 02:52.062
we can bring back
nine ounces.

02:52.064 --> 02:53.764
Fire up the jet.

02:55.166 --> 02:57.634
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

02:57.636 --> 02:59.727
♪ Ah.
♪ Men.

02:59.728 --> 03:02.728
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 11x21 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Dial 1-900-Mix-A-Lot&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on May 1,

03:02.729 --> 03:07.729
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

03:07.730 --> 03:09.331
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

03:09.333 --> 03:14.503
Well, guess who just joined
the Mile High Club.

03:14.514 --> 03:17.282
No, it doesn't count
when you do it alone.

03:17.284 --> 03:20.452
Oh, it counted... twice.

03:20.454 --> 03:21.787
Up top.

03:21.789 --> 03:22.921
No!

03:22.923 --> 03:24.256
Not gonna happen.

03:25.758 --> 03:27.059
This is crazy.

03:27.061 --> 03:29.361
There's no way my old car
is worth the cost

03:29.363 --> 03:32.431
of flying all the way to Denver
and putting in a new bathroom.

03:34.434 --> 03:35.868
We can't turn back now.

03:35.870 --> 03:37.603
I canceled an audition
for this trip.

03:37.605 --> 03:38.937
You're kidding, right?

03:38.939 --> 03:41.874
The part was
Dead Junkie Number Two.

03:41.876 --> 03:46.011
Although, I did buy painkillers
to get into character.

03:46.013 --> 03:48.780
It doesn't matter
what the role is.

03:48.782 --> 03:50.983
This job leads to the next,

03:50.985 --> 03:53.719
and you're playing
Dead Junkie Number One.

03:53.721 --> 03:56.555
And before you know it,
you're playing a live junkie!

03:56.557 --> 03:58.223
And then what?

03:58.225 --> 03:59.558
Win a bunch of Oscars,

03:59.560 --> 04:02.294
get rich, fly around
on a private plane?

04:02.296 --> 04:04.396
Oh, look, I skipped to the end!

04:04.398 --> 04:06.665
So what kind of car
are we going to look at?

04:06.667 --> 04:09.001
You can thank me later
for changing the subject.

04:10.069 --> 04:12.104
It's a 1967 Mustang

04:12.106 --> 04:14.873
with a 289 V-8,
a Holley four-barrel carb

04:14.875 --> 04:15.974
and Positraction.

04:15.976 --> 04:17.142
(whistles)

04:17.144 --> 04:18.544
What does that mean?

04:18.546 --> 04:21.914
I have no idea. My dad used
to say it all the time

04:21.916 --> 04:23.649
when we were working on the car.

04:24.617 --> 04:25.784
I like to think that it

04:25.786 --> 04:28.186
was one of his ways
of saying, "I love you."

04:28.188 --> 04:30.155
Another was,
"Why is Daddy's beer empty?"

04:30.157 --> 04:31.356
I totally get it.

04:31.358 --> 04:33.725
My dad's coded "I love you"
was, "Seriously?

04:33.727 --> 04:35.894
You can't catch a football
one damn time?"

04:35.896 --> 04:37.696
(chuckles)

04:38.965 --> 04:41.266
So you worked on this
with your dad.

04:41.268 --> 04:43.702
Apparently, there's an emotional
connection with this car.

04:43.704 --> 04:45.037
It's a mixed emotion.

04:45.039 --> 04:47.906
It took us two years
to restore it.

04:47.908 --> 04:50.576
When it was finished,
it was cherry.

04:50.578 --> 04:53.011
Of course, Cherry was also
the name of the stripper

04:53.013 --> 04:55.814
that he drove off with
when he left me and my mom.

04:55.816 --> 04:57.683
Wait-- so why would you
want to buy something

04:57.685 --> 04:59.051
that caused you
so much pain?

04:59.053 --> 05:01.119
I mean, that'd be like me buying
the senior prom.

05:02.989 --> 05:05.190
It was on my 16th birthday.

05:05.192 --> 05:08.427
I go outside the house...
and there's that car

05:08.429 --> 05:10.062
sitting in the driveway.

05:10.064 --> 05:11.597
No sign of my dad, though.

05:11.599 --> 05:13.098
It was still the best
birthday ever.

05:13.100 --> 05:15.634
Well, until my mom took a
baseball bat to the windshield.

05:15.636 --> 05:18.403
You know what my dad got me
for my 16th birthday?

05:18.405 --> 05:20.405
A box of condoms and a card
that said,

05:20.407 --> 05:22.474
"Don't make the same mistake
I did."

05:23.743 --> 05:25.143
He was a joker.

05:26.379 --> 05:27.980
How about you, Jenny?

05:29.415 --> 05:32.417
Oh, she would've nailed
Dead Junkie Number Two!

05:33.620 --> 05:35.654
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

05:35.656 --> 05:37.389
Oh! What a great idea:

05:37.391 --> 05:39.691
having sex in every
room in the house.

05:39.693 --> 05:42.327
Well, to be fair,
the laundry room was more you

05:42.329 --> 05:44.529
sitting on the dryer
while I took a breather.

05:44.531 --> 05:45.664
Yeah. Next time, I think

05:45.666 --> 05:47.733
I'm gonna throw in
a pair of snow boots.

05:47.735 --> 05:50.435
You know, boom-boom-boom-boom-boom!
Yeah.

05:50.437 --> 05:53.705
One of the advantages
of being here alone.

05:53.707 --> 05:56.408
Kind of makes a man want
to buy a place of his own.

05:56.410 --> 05:58.777
(both laugh)

05:59.612 --> 06:01.913
Nah, I'm gonna die here,
I really am.

06:01.915 --> 06:04.383
So, uh, what do you want
to do tonight?

06:04.385 --> 06:06.218
You know,
besides this guy.

06:06.220 --> 06:08.754
I would love to spend
the night doing this guy,

06:08.756 --> 06:10.889
but we promised Lyndsey and Larry
we'd meet 'em.

06:10.891 --> 06:11.923
Remember, karaoke?

06:11.925 --> 06:12.991
Oh, that's right.

06:12.993 --> 06:14.860
Oh, hey, hey,
maybe we can use

06:14.862 --> 06:16.194
my Halloween costumes
from last year.

06:16.196 --> 06:17.829
You know, Donny and Marie?

06:17.831 --> 06:20.766
Although I'm not sure you'd fit
into Walden's Donny outfit.

06:21.868 --> 06:25.671
You know, I was thinking
tonight would be a great time

06:25.673 --> 06:27.706
to tell Larry that you're
not Jeff Strongman,

06:27.708 --> 06:29.141
that you're really
Alan Harper.

06:29.143 --> 06:31.109
Oh, that's funny
because I was thinking

06:31.111 --> 06:34.713
tonight might be a great night
to not ruin four people's lives.

06:34.715 --> 06:35.847
He's my brother, Alan.

06:35.849 --> 06:37.482
I can't just
keep lying to him.

06:37.484 --> 06:39.851
I lied to my brother all
the time. It worked out great.

06:39.853 --> 06:41.420
Your brother's dead.

06:41.422 --> 06:44.222
I didn't say it worked out
great for everybody.

06:45.091 --> 06:46.792
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

06:46.794 --> 06:47.926
(plays discordant chord)

06:47.928 --> 06:49.094
Hey!

06:50.329 --> 06:51.496
Are you Dirk?

06:51.498 --> 06:52.731
Are you a cop?

06:52.733 --> 06:54.900
No.
Then I'm Dirk.

06:54.902 --> 06:56.835
I'm Walden Schmidt.
I called about the car.

06:56.837 --> 06:59.071
Actually, on the phone,
you asked if I was a cop.

06:59.073 --> 07:01.540
And then you asked me
if I wanted to buy any weed.

07:01.542 --> 07:04.176
Yeah, that's the right order
to ask those questions.

07:04.178 --> 07:05.944
I learned that the hard way.

07:07.113 --> 07:08.013
These your kids?

07:08.015 --> 07:09.414
(snickers)

07:09.416 --> 07:11.316
No.

07:11.318 --> 07:12.617
Are they mine?

07:14.187 --> 07:15.821
Hey, uh, is this the car?

07:15.823 --> 07:18.557
Yeah, let me take her
top off for you.

07:18.559 --> 07:21.293
You're about to see one hot car.

07:24.063 --> 07:26.164
Where, behind
this piece of crap?

07:26.166 --> 07:28.834
She's not that pretty,
but she gets the job done.

07:28.836 --> 07:30.936
Just like my old lady.

07:30.938 --> 07:32.270
Hey, that's not bad.

07:32.272 --> 07:34.973
♪ She's not that pretty,
but she gets the job done ♪

07:34.975 --> 07:39.010
♪ I'd like to escape,
but I'm too old to run! ♪

07:39.012 --> 07:40.612
Yeah, that's a hit!

07:41.647 --> 07:43.415
So is this your car?

07:43.417 --> 07:44.850
Yeah.

07:44.852 --> 07:47.753
It's still got the Vote For Bush
bumper sticker on it.

07:47.755 --> 07:49.121
You were a Republican?

07:49.123 --> 07:51.590
No, my friends and I
just thought it was funny.

07:51.592 --> 07:53.725
You know, "Bush"?

07:53.727 --> 07:57.429
Tell you what, I love Bush.

07:57.431 --> 07:59.331
You and me both.

08:00.733 --> 08:02.834
She's got a lot
of wear and tear on her.

08:02.836 --> 08:04.603
Not much to look at.

08:04.605 --> 08:06.404
Looks like it was rear-ended.

08:06.406 --> 08:08.340
Just like my old lady.

08:09.942 --> 08:12.511
But she's got new headlights
and a roomy backseat.

08:12.513 --> 08:13.779
Just like your old lady?

08:13.781 --> 08:17.048
Hey! That's the mother
of three of my five kids!

08:18.451 --> 08:21.019
Anyway, this bad boy can still
get up to a buck ten.

08:21.021 --> 08:23.989
Yeah, maybe if the truck
towing it was going 110.

08:23.991 --> 08:26.158
You don't believe me,
I refer you

08:26.160 --> 08:29.828
to &lt;i>World's Wildest&lt;/i>
&lt;i>Police Chases,&lt;/i> episode 139.

08:31.063 --> 08:32.564
Whoa, what died in here?

08:32.566 --> 08:34.666
My granddad.

08:34.668 --> 08:36.134
The seat belt got jammed,
we had to

08:36.136 --> 08:38.103
leave him in there
for a couple of days.

08:39.705 --> 08:42.641
Okay, well, hey, thank you
for showing us the car.

08:42.643 --> 08:44.075
Whoa, hang on, hang on.

08:44.911 --> 08:46.044
How much do
you want for it?

08:46.046 --> 08:47.879
Uh, uh, uh, what are you doing?

08:48.981 --> 08:50.549
I'll take $1,800 unless you can

08:50.551 --> 08:52.551
come up with some kind
of other arrangement.

08:52.553 --> 08:53.718
Ew!

08:53.720 --> 08:55.387
How about you?

08:55.389 --> 08:58.256
No!

08:58.258 --> 09:00.725
$1,800 it is, then.

09:00.727 --> 09:03.929
I'm not...
I'm not buying this car.

09:03.931 --> 09:06.131
Walden, this car
is a piece of your life.

09:06.133 --> 09:07.666
It doesn't mean anything
to anybody else

09:07.668 --> 09:09.067
in the world except you.

09:10.937 --> 09:13.205
All right, I'll give you $1,800.

09:13.207 --> 09:16.641
Dude, you didn't haggle.
It's no good unless you haggle.

09:16.643 --> 09:20.145
Okay, uh, fine. $1,600.

09:20.147 --> 09:21.146
$1,700.

09:21.148 --> 09:23.114
Deal. $1,700.

09:23.116 --> 09:25.083
Yeah!

09:26.285 --> 09:27.953
I was just gonna give you
$1,800.

09:27.955 --> 09:29.788
That's the thing
about haggling, dude.

09:29.790 --> 09:32.591
Sometimes you win,
sometimes you lose.

09:33.960 --> 09:35.994
We definitely have to get
some of this guy's weed.

09:35.996 --> 09:38.129
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:39.765 --> 09:42.901
♪ Hey, will you love me
forever? ♪

09:42.903 --> 09:45.403
♪ Let me sleep on it

09:45.405 --> 09:46.504
♪ Will you love me forever?

09:46.506 --> 09:48.139
♪ Let me sleep on it

09:48.141 --> 09:49.875
♪ Will you love me forever?

09:49.877 --> 09:51.343
♪ I couldn't take it
any longer ♪

09:51.345 --> 09:52.744
♪ Lord, I was crazed

09:52.746 --> 09:55.247
♪ And then the feeling came
upon me like a tidal wave ♪

09:55.249 --> 09:57.782
♪ I started swearing to my God
on my mother's grave ♪

09:57.784 --> 10:00.518
♪ That I would love you
till the end of time ♪

10:00.520 --> 10:03.622
♪ I swore I'd love you
till the end of time! ♪

10:03.624 --> 10:05.257
Yeah!

10:05.259 --> 10:06.858
Gretchen, Jeff!

10:06.860 --> 10:09.628
Follow that, bitches.

10:09.630 --> 10:11.696
Come on, Lyndsey, it's our turn.

10:11.698 --> 10:13.565
♪ Who let the dogs out?

10:13.567 --> 10:16.501
Woof, woof. Woof, woof.

10:16.503 --> 10:18.336
Come on. You can do
better than that.

10:18.338 --> 10:20.772
Larry, do I look like I want
to do better than that?

10:20.774 --> 10:22.407
Ooh, last time I saw
that face,

10:22.409 --> 10:24.676
I forgot
to pick up wine.

10:24.678 --> 10:26.311
Boy, was I in
the doghouse

10:26.313 --> 10:27.412
that night. Hey!

10:27.414 --> 10:30.282
♪ Who's in the doghouse?

10:30.284 --> 10:32.284
♪ Who-who-who-who?

10:32.286 --> 10:33.351
That's what
I'm talking about!

10:33.353 --> 10:34.619
Come on. Let's show 'em how

10:34.621 --> 10:36.488
you and your brother
do it doggy style.

10:39.325 --> 10:42.127
He doesn't really
hear himself, does he?

10:42.129 --> 10:44.562
Why are you here?

10:44.564 --> 10:46.431
I've told you a hundred times,
I don't want

10:46.433 --> 10:48.300
to double-date with Gretchen
and Jeff Strongman.

10:48.302 --> 10:50.568
Well, you won't
have to anymore.

10:50.570 --> 10:52.270
Guess who's gonna tell Larry
the truth tonight.

10:52.272 --> 10:54.973
♪ Who-who-who-who?

10:56.776 --> 10:57.876
What do you mean?

10:57.878 --> 11:00.545
I told Gretchen
who I really am.

11:00.547 --> 11:02.781
I was tired of living a lie

11:02.783 --> 11:03.982
and sneaking around,
being dishonest.

11:03.984 --> 11:05.050
I'm better than that.

11:05.052 --> 11:06.251
She caught you.

11:06.253 --> 11:07.585
Yes. Yes, she did.

11:07.587 --> 11:09.921
But it felt good
to get it off my chest.

11:09.923 --> 11:13.158
If you tell Larry
who you really are,

11:13.160 --> 11:15.527
then he's gonna wonder why
I didn't tell him.

11:15.529 --> 11:17.362
And that's not something
I want to deal with

11:17.364 --> 11:19.531
less than two weeks before
we're supposed to get married.

11:19.533 --> 11:20.865
God, is it two weeks?

11:20.867 --> 11:22.567
Boy, I better find
those rings.

11:22.569 --> 11:25.103
Alan, you're not gonna say
a thing about

11:25.105 --> 11:26.371
who you really are.

11:26.373 --> 11:28.073
I'm sorry, but I already
promised Gretchen.

11:28.075 --> 11:29.607
And-and the fact
of the matter is

11:29.609 --> 11:31.309
you and I aren't
in a relationship anymore,

11:31.311 --> 11:34.479
so you no longer have me
by the &lt;i>balls!&lt;/i>

11:41.625 --> 11:43.059
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:43.061 --> 11:46.028
♪ Dial 1-900-mix-a-lot
and kick them nasty thoughts ♪

11:46.030 --> 11:47.730
♪ Baby got back!

11:48.999 --> 11:50.266
(cheering)

11:52.169 --> 11:55.238
Come on, Larry, let's
show 'em how we do it.

11:55.240 --> 11:56.973
There you go!

11:56.975 --> 11:59.242
Menstrual cramps
can't stop my lady!

11:59.244 --> 12:01.377
It's Larry-oke time!

12:06.049 --> 12:08.184
♪ Ow! I feel good

12:09.786 --> 12:11.520
♪ I knew that I would now

12:11.522 --> 12:14.223
So, did you talk
to Larry yet?

12:14.225 --> 12:16.092
Uh, well, you know,
I was, I was running

12:16.094 --> 12:17.593
this whole thing by
Lyndsey, and, um...

12:17.595 --> 12:21.097
Whoa, wait. Why would you
run it by Lyndsey?

12:21.099 --> 12:22.331
You know, she is the
one getting married,

12:22.333 --> 12:23.799
and I didn't want
to spring it on her

12:23.801 --> 12:25.635
because Lyndsey is not the
girl you want to get angry

12:25.637 --> 12:26.969
unless you're about
to have sex with her,

12:26.971 --> 12:28.638
'cause then she
turns into a freak,

12:28.640 --> 12:30.239
and I don't know
why I'm saying this.

12:30.241 --> 12:31.307
I know why.

12:31.309 --> 12:33.209
Because you still have
feelings for her.

12:33.211 --> 12:34.810
(scoffs) That's crazy.
I just, I think

12:34.812 --> 12:36.612
it's the right thing to do,
that's all.

12:36.614 --> 12:39.548
Oh, my God.

12:39.550 --> 12:41.617
That is why you invented
Jeff Strongman

12:41.619 --> 12:44.620
in the first place,
was to win Lyndsey back.

12:44.622 --> 12:46.889
Feelings like that
don't just disappear.

12:46.891 --> 12:48.591
Sure, they do.
There's a lot of things

12:48.593 --> 12:50.559
I used to love that
I don't love anymore:

12:50.561 --> 12:52.595
uh, roller coasters,
dairy, my mother.

12:52.597 --> 12:54.330
This isn't funny, Alan.

12:54.332 --> 12:55.298
Well, I-I was just saying...

12:55.300 --> 12:56.732
No, listen to me.

12:56.734 --> 13:00.269
Look, if you want to run
everything by your ex-girlfriend

13:00.271 --> 13:02.405
and not tell Larry the truth,
then so be it.

13:02.407 --> 13:04.247
But I don't want anything
to do with it. Or you.

13:04.272 --> 13:04.908
Wait, Gretchen...

13:04.909 --> 13:07.677
Gretchen. Gretchen, wait!

13:07.679 --> 13:09.679
♪ I feel good

13:11.081 --> 13:12.915
♪ I knew that I would now

13:12.917 --> 13:15.051
Come on, Jeff,
you know the words.

13:15.053 --> 13:18.187
♪ So good, so good

13:18.189 --> 13:19.555
♪ I'm gonna die alone

13:19.557 --> 13:21.457
♪ Ow!

13:22.259 --> 13:24.160
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

13:24.162 --> 13:26.195
Aren't you glad
I made you do this?

13:26.197 --> 13:29.298
Yeah.
Having déjà vu.

13:29.300 --> 13:32.234
My dad used to let me sit
on his lap and steer.

13:32.236 --> 13:33.903
Yeah, my dad
wasn't around much.

13:33.905 --> 13:36.973
I had to teach myself all those
things that dads teach you:

13:36.975 --> 13:39.041
how to ride a bike,
how to shave,

13:39.043 --> 13:41.944
how to change a tire,
how to masturbate.

13:41.946 --> 13:43.679
What?

13:43.681 --> 13:46.315
No, dads don't teach you
how to masturbate.

13:46.317 --> 13:50.152
I'm glad somebody told me
before I had kids.

13:50.154 --> 13:52.121
This thing is actually
really cool.

13:52.123 --> 13:54.156
What made you sell it
in the first place?

13:54.158 --> 13:56.192
I needed the seed money
to start my company,

13:56.194 --> 13:59.495
and it's the only thing
I had that was worth anything.

13:59.497 --> 14:02.131
You know,
when you think about it,

14:02.133 --> 14:04.433
this car is really responsible
for everything I have:

14:04.435 --> 14:08.170
the beach house,
my jet and my fortune.

14:08.172 --> 14:09.338
Alan.

14:09.340 --> 14:12.908
Shh, she didn't mean it.
It's not true.

14:12.910 --> 14:16.645
So that means your dad
is kind of responsible

14:16.647 --> 14:18.280
for your success, too,
doesn't it?

14:18.282 --> 14:21.283
I never really thought of it
like that.

14:21.285 --> 14:24.620
I guess he is.

14:24.622 --> 14:26.255
Thanks, Dad.

14:26.257 --> 14:28.924
Oh, that gave me the chills.

14:28.926 --> 14:29.925
Oh! No, wait.

14:29.927 --> 14:32.495
There's a hole
in the floorboard.

14:35.565 --> 14:37.833
Anybody else want to
drive for a while?

14:37.835 --> 14:40.169
I don't know how to drive.

14:40.171 --> 14:42.038
What?

14:42.040 --> 14:43.606
I grew up in Manhattan.

14:43.608 --> 14:45.541
I've been in taxis and cop cars.

14:45.543 --> 14:48.878
Ooh, this is my first time
in the front seat!

14:49.913 --> 14:52.882
Well, there's no time
like the present.

14:52.884 --> 14:54.617
(all screaming)

14:58.588 --> 15:00.556
I'm gonna pull
in here.

15:00.558 --> 15:03.459
I'm pretty sure they sell underwear
at Cracker Barrel.

15:05.162 --> 15:08.631
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:08.633 --> 15:10.132
Berta?

15:10.134 --> 15:12.068
Hey, Zippy.

15:12.070 --> 15:13.436
It's 10:00.

15:13.438 --> 15:14.870
What are you still doing here?

15:14.872 --> 15:16.439
It's 11 years later.

15:16.441 --> 15:18.808
What are you
still doing here?

15:20.277 --> 15:21.577
Where's your girlfriend?

15:21.579 --> 15:24.313
Gone. I think I lost her.

15:24.315 --> 15:26.515
You mean "lost"
like you broke up

15:26.517 --> 15:29.985
or "lost" like the time Charlie
took Jake to Disneyland?

15:29.987 --> 15:33.055
Broke up.
Wait-- Charlie lost Jake?

15:33.057 --> 15:34.990
Actually, Jake lost Charlie.

15:35.892 --> 15:37.026
Security found him.

15:37.028 --> 15:39.395
He was doing white snow
with Snow White.

15:40.797 --> 15:41.931
So, um,

15:41.933 --> 15:45.267
what did you do to drive
this girlfriend away?

15:45.269 --> 15:47.136
She thinks I'm still
in love with Lyndsey,

15:47.138 --> 15:49.839
which I'm not,
but she doesn't believe me.

15:49.841 --> 15:51.273
Well, make her believe you.

15:51.275 --> 15:53.476
You can make anybody believe
anything.

15:53.478 --> 15:56.312
You made the IRS believe
you had seven dependents.

15:56.314 --> 15:58.247
That's true.

15:58.249 --> 16:01.484
I went to chiropractic college
on an NAACP scholarship.

16:03.854 --> 16:05.187
Exactly.

16:05.189 --> 16:07.623
And you made those people
at the movie theater

16:07.625 --> 16:09.425
believe that you were under 14.

16:10.694 --> 16:13.062
And over 65.

16:13.064 --> 16:14.463
Once on the same day.

16:14.465 --> 16:15.631
(laughs)

16:15.633 --> 16:18.167
The, uh, the secret is
that both of those groups wear

16:18.169 --> 16:20.936
little baseball caps.
(laughs)

16:20.938 --> 16:23.539
I was saving this
for your funeral,

16:23.541 --> 16:25.741
but, Zippy, you're a charmer.

16:25.743 --> 16:27.409
Thanks, Berta.

16:27.411 --> 16:29.011
No. Thank you.

16:29.013 --> 16:31.847
Now I don't have
to go to your funeral.

16:32.883 --> 16:36.051
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

16:36.053 --> 16:37.853
Wow,

16:37.855 --> 16:41.690
this Utah sky is amazing.

16:41.692 --> 16:43.726
We're indoors.

16:43.728 --> 16:48.797
Wow, this Colorado weed
is amazing.

16:50.467 --> 16:54.737
Guess who just joined
the 6,106-foot club.

16:54.739 --> 16:58.941
It doesn't count
when you do it alone!

16:58.943 --> 17:00.442
Whatever.

17:00.444 --> 17:01.744
I don't like it here.

17:01.746 --> 17:03.812
There's no Wi-Fi
or cell service.

17:03.814 --> 17:05.881
It's like one of those movies
where you find out

17:05.883 --> 17:07.249
the little town's full
of zombies.

17:07.251 --> 17:09.285
Or werewolves.

17:09.287 --> 17:10.753
Or zombie werewolves.

17:10.755 --> 17:12.221
How would that happen?

17:12.223 --> 17:13.923
Hello. Do the math.

17:13.925 --> 17:15.090
Zombie bites a werewolf,

17:15.092 --> 17:16.959
werewolf dies, comes back
as a werewolf zombie.

17:16.961 --> 17:19.061
That's a badass,
unkillable creature.

17:19.063 --> 17:20.396
He's right. Chain the door.

17:20.398 --> 17:22.765
Wait a second. You think
chaining the door

17:22.767 --> 17:25.167
is gonna stop
a zombie werewolf?

17:25.169 --> 17:27.770
I'll tell you what,
I'm not gonna be the guy

17:27.772 --> 17:29.405
who gets killed by
a zombie werewolf

17:29.407 --> 17:31.740
'cause I didn't chain the door.

17:33.210 --> 17:35.744
(laughs)
Hey...

17:35.746 --> 17:37.279
thanks for coming with me, guys.

17:37.281 --> 17:38.647
And I'm not just saying that

17:38.649 --> 17:40.416
'cause I can use you
as human shields

17:40.418 --> 17:42.384
when the zombie werewolf
breaks in the door.

17:42.386 --> 17:45.054
Yeah, I'm really
glad we came, too.

17:45.056 --> 17:47.089
And about almost
killing you guys

17:47.091 --> 17:50.092
in the car earlier--
that's my bad.

17:50.094 --> 17:51.360
Yeah, well, I am glad

17:51.362 --> 17:53.929
that Cracker Barrel
had underwear.

17:54.898 --> 17:57.833
And these "I Heart Denver"
sweatpants.

17:58.868 --> 18:01.103
You know, this is still better
than that family trip

18:01.105 --> 18:02.638
I took to Utah
as a kid.

18:02.640 --> 18:04.340
My dad was trying
to convince my mom

18:04.342 --> 18:05.941
to add another wife
to the family.

18:05.943 --> 18:07.376
Started the trip
with one wife,

18:07.378 --> 18:09.345
tried to get two,
came home with zero.

18:10.614 --> 18:13.949
Hotel had
a great pool, though.

18:13.951 --> 18:15.985
At least you knew
your dad.

18:15.987 --> 18:17.920
I barely knew Charlie.

18:17.922 --> 18:21.090
I got one letter from him
my entire childhood.

18:21.092 --> 18:24.326
It said, "Are your
friends 18 yet""

18:24.328 --> 18:27.529
Yeah, hearing you guys talk
about your dads,

18:27.531 --> 18:29.098
and thinking about mine,

18:29.100 --> 18:30.833
makes me question even wanting
to have kids.

18:30.835 --> 18:32.835
You already have kids.

18:32.837 --> 18:34.069
(Walden laughs)

18:34.071 --> 18:35.938
Papa.

18:37.007 --> 18:38.374
Come on. I'm not your dad.

18:38.376 --> 18:42.478
You've been a better dad
to me than anybody ever has.

18:42.480 --> 18:44.613
You-you-you took me in,

18:44.615 --> 18:48.284
you inspired me to be
a better person.

18:48.286 --> 18:51.587
You pushed me to be
a dead junkie.

18:51.589 --> 18:54.790
I really want that for you, too.

18:54.792 --> 18:56.759
She's right, man.
You're a role model.

18:56.761 --> 18:58.093
I mean, you believe that

18:58.095 --> 18:59.895
I can make something
out of myself

18:59.897 --> 19:01.630
and you stopped me
from going to prison

19:01.632 --> 19:03.399
for teaching my son
how to masturbate.

19:04.401 --> 19:07.336
That's right.
You want to be a hands-on dad,

19:07.338 --> 19:09.638
but not too hands-on.

19:11.207 --> 19:13.809
Hey, bring it in, kiddos.

19:15.245 --> 19:16.478
Oh!
Aw...

19:16.480 --> 19:18.347
(laughs)

19:18.349 --> 19:20.516
Oh, Dad?
Hmm?

19:20.518 --> 19:23.018
Barry's got his hand
on my butt again.

19:24.054 --> 19:25.387
It's not my hand.
Okay.

19:25.389 --> 19:26.789
All right.

19:26.791 --> 19:29.358
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

19:29.360 --> 19:31.527
(doorbell rings)

19:33.530 --> 19:34.663
Hey, Gretchie.

19:34.665 --> 19:36.699
I don't want to talk
to you right now.

19:36.701 --> 19:38.867
Gretchen's still mad at you,
but I'm on your side, Jeff.

19:38.869 --> 19:41.837
Bros before hoes.

19:41.839 --> 19:44.506
Oh, uh, oh, good, you're,
uh, you're all here.

19:44.508 --> 19:47.343
Because I have something
to say...

19:47.345 --> 19:48.711
to everyone.

19:48.713 --> 19:50.212
Are you sure, Jeff?

19:50.214 --> 19:53.048
Some things
are better left unsaid.

19:54.651 --> 19:56.051
I love you so much,

19:56.053 --> 19:58.420
I-I can't imagine
my life without you.

19:58.422 --> 19:59.688
Just stop.

19:59.690 --> 20:01.657
Maybe this will help.

20:01.659 --> 20:03.158
Okay, I appreciate the gesture,

20:03.160 --> 20:06.161
but looking for change together
isn't gonna work this time.

20:06.163 --> 20:10.499
The only change I want is
for us to be husband and wife.

20:10.501 --> 20:12.434
ALL:
What?!

20:12.436 --> 20:15.237
Gretchen Martin,
will you do me the honor

20:15.239 --> 20:20.109
of becoming Mrs. Alan Harper?

20:21.644 --> 20:24.580
Oh, my God!
My sister and my best...

20:24.582 --> 20:26.882
Wait a minute.
Who the hell is Alan Harper?

20:26.884 --> 20:29.318
Larry, look, boobs!

20:29.320 --> 20:31.487
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:37.108 --> 20:38.208
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:38.210 --> 20:39.743
Oh, look at you.
You're doing great.

20:39.745 --> 20:41.244
You haven't hit
a guardrail in miles.

20:42.491 --> 20:43.926
Once you get
the hang of it,

20:43.927 --> 20:45.426
this driving thing
isn't so tough.

20:45.428 --> 20:48.563
How about after I restore it,
I give it to you?

20:48.565 --> 20:50.331
What? You love this car.

20:50.333 --> 20:52.133
I've gotten what
I need out of it,

20:52.135 --> 20:54.368
and I'd rather have it
stay in the family.

20:54.370 --> 20:56.270
Who better to have it
than my my...

20:56.272 --> 20:57.371
sort-of-daughter.

20:57.373 --> 21:00.374
Aw! You're the best
sort-of-dad ever!

21:00.376 --> 21:01.743
Whoa! Hands on the wheel!

21:01.745 --> 21:04.178
Hands on the wheel!
(tires squealing)

21:04.180 --> 21:05.880
Whoa!
Why are you yelling at me?

21:05.882 --> 21:07.181
You should be
yelling at them

21:07.183 --> 21:08.549
for driving on
the wrong side...

21:08.551 --> 21:09.917
(all scream)

21:09.919 --> 21:14.919
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>
